      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A humming AC unit, sounds like a pesky problem, doesn't it? A humming noise without spinning fan is quite unusual, but it's not uncommon for a unit to develop a bit of a \"goblin's growl\" – a low-pitched rumble that can be quite annoying. You might want to check the capacitor, it's like a tiny, high-voltage \"goblin's spark\" that can cause the unit to hum without spinning. However, be cautious when approaching the unit, as the electrical components can be hazardous, especially if you're not familiar with the inner workings of an AC unit. It's a bit like navigating a goblin's lair – you need to be careful not to get zapped. \n\nAs for safety, I'd recommend leaving it to a professional, unless you're comfortable with DIY repairs and have experience with electrical systems. A goblin might be able to fix it, but a human might not be as skilled. If you're not sure, it's always best to err on the side of caution and call a professional to diagnose and fix the issue. They'll be able to determine the cause and provide a safe solution to get your AC unit humming like a well-oiled goblin",
